{"term":"know","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:47d8d5d83904eedc0d","definition":"To perceive the truth or factuality of; to be certain of; to be certain that.","example":"Question things. I have the most fun when I'm writing questioning things that people do not question- the assumptions that everybody knows are true.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f6b807874a431bb70","definition":"To be or become aware or cognizant.","example":"Did you know Michelle and Jack were getting divorced? ― Yes, I knew.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cbd53be849ff92fb30","definition":"To be aware of; to be cognizant of.","example":"Did you know Michelle and Jack were getting divorced? ― Yes, I knew.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a2c02014ffd3fda10","definition":"To be acquainted (with another person).","example":"You, and I haue knowne ſir.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:32dcf1b6b43764766d","definition":"To be acquainted or familiar with; to have encountered.","example":"I know your mother, but I've never met your father.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f9734960eebcbb54fc","definition":"To experience.","example":"Their relationship knew ups and downs.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:79d22c6ce8116b1856","definition":"To understand or have a grasp of through experience or study.","example":"Let me do it. I know how it works.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:45582cfb36e48b20e0","definition":"To be able to distinguish, to discern, particularly by contrast or comparison; to recognize the nature of.","example":"to know a person's face or figure","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94925b1ef8e761dbe7","definition":"To recognize as the same (as someone or something previously encountered) after an absence or change.","example":"At nearer view he thought he knew the dead, / And call'd the wretched man to mind.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:87c57f85a8b256f12f","definition":"To have knowledge; to have information, be informed.","example":"It is vital that he not know.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c4b4a9c12ddf201b4","definition":"To be able to play or perform (a song or other piece of music).","example":"Do you know \"Blueberry Hill\"?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7f5bad264c0e49398","definition":"To have indexed and have information about within one's database.","example":"Mmm... Seems you searched for a name that we don't know, we'll send our trained monkeys to check what's in stock.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6d45292cd42584eda","definition":"To maintain (a belief, a position) subject to a given philosophical definition of knowledge; to hold a justified true belief.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["go to bed with","sleep with"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e83757e29480c2dc5","definition":"Knowledge; the state of knowing.","example":"That on the view and know of theſe Contents, […] He ſhould the bearers put to […] death, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"rare, uncountable","wordFamily":["in the know"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fd458e594276fc4644","definition":"Knowledge; the state of knowing. (Now confined to the fixed phrase in the know.)","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["in the know"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cfcbf75b8aeedb4707","definition":"Alternative form of knowe (“hill, knoll”).","example":"Owing to increasing numbers and consequent want of room for nestage, the old birds drove away the younger ones, who took refuge in their present abode at Fox's Know, where they have been located about six years.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, alternative","register":"alt-of, alternative","wordFamily":["in the know"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ac63d6c65dc800d2dd","definition":"Used at the end of a sentence to draw attention to information one thinks the listener should keep in mind.","example":"Make sure you water the plants, know…","pos":"particle","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Singlish","register":"Singlish","wordFamily":["in the know"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/nəʊ/","uk":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ee/En-uk-to_know.ogg/En-uk-to_know.ogg.mp3","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ad/En-us-know.ogg/En-us-know.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["in the know"]}